WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.640
We need to see women embracing AI, so let's talk about why we cannot afford to leave women behind

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:08.000
and the technology that is shaping the future of economics and ethics.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.080
There is an existing gender gap in AI usage and leadership. Women are statistically much

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:16.000
more skeptical of AI and use it much less, with research from a Harvard Business School

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:21.760
associate professor finding that women are adopting AI tools at a 25% lower rate than men.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:26.320
Women are statistically more skeptical of AI and use it much less, with research from a Harvard

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:29.680
Business School associate professor finding that women are adopting AI tools

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:34.520
at a 25% lower rate than men. In the workforce women make up only one in four

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:37.920
new AI hires and that representation declines further up the corporate ladder.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:42.240
Just one in seven AI executives are women with even fewer women founding

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:46.040
their own AI companies. These numbers are a problem. By staying out of AI women are

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:49.160
keeping themselves out of decision rooms that their voices need to be heard in

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:52.040
and limiting themselves from key economic opportunities that are

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:56.670
essential for achieving gender economic equality. One of the biggest reasons so

00:00:56.670 --> 00:00:59.750
many women are keeping themselves out of AI is because women are more likely to

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:03.590
have concerns surrounding the ethics of AI technologies and these are valid

00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:07.230
concerns. AI has the potential to be very dangerous but it's also not going away

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:11.710
anytime soon. We need to see women understanding AI, using AI, and leading AI

00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:14.850
if we want to see women leading conversations about regulations,

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:19.070
safeguards, and morality regarding these technologies. Because when it comes to

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:23.110
ethics and AI, we need women in the center of these conversations. I do not

00:01:23.110 --> 00:01:26.270
trust a roomful of men to make the right moral decisions, especially when there's

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:30.290
profit on the line. Profit and economics is also a huge conversation that needs

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:34.510
to be had. AI is the future of big business and economic prosperity, and how

00:01:34.510 --> 00:01:38.410
women go about using AI in the coming years has the potential to define the

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:42.170
future of female wealth and female power. It was not that long ago that women

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:45.690
finally gained the right to open bank accounts and obtain credit cards in

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:49.330
their own name. Women today are still fighting to close the economic gap

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:53.370
created by generations of inequality. And we cannot afford to let the

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:57.930
technological revolution be another setback in women's progress. AI is

00:01:57.930 --> 00:02:01.290
shaping the future and women need a seat at the table in deciding what the future

00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:06.290
looks like. So ladies, do not sit this one out. Embrace AI, lead in it, and help

00:02:06.290 --> 00:02:11.210
shape the world that it creates. That's all she wrote. Bye guys!
